WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.869
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module,

2
00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:05.450
which takes about fifty-five
minutes with the lab.

3
00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:07.681
You'll name the five
closure conditions and

4
00:00:07.681 --> 00:00:10.025
the fields the closure
record shows for each.

5
00:00:10.025 --> 00:00:12.906
You'll explain why two
fields are always external,

6
00:00:12.906 --> 00:00:17.262
and why a record with nothing not met is
ready for the assessor, never closed.

7
00:00:17.262 --> 00:00:20.953
You'll run the kit's closure record
and drift comparison on the day-one

8
00:00:20.953 --> 00:00:24.450
and day-thirty fixtures, with and
without the exception registry.

9
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:26.818
And you'll say what the
drift check catches,

10
00:00:26.818 --> 00:00:30.200
and why Arc going offline needs
an Arc snapshot with each run.

11
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.662
Before you start, finish Module 8.

12
00:00:32.662 --> 00:00:37.780
The closure record reads the audit from
Module 2 and the Arc snapshot from Module 3.
